PN,31402
SC,0002
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F314A1785383018
OL,3,C'Highly dangerous' travel adaptors
OL,4,Cfound for sale to UK consumers
OL,6,FThe charity warned that information
OL,7,Favailable on the listings suggested
OL,8,Fmore than 10,000 of the unsafe
OL,9,Fadaptors may have already been sold to
OL,10,FUK shoppers.
OL,12,FIn six of eight universal travel
OL,13,Fadaptors tested, more than one set of
OL,14,Fplug pins could be exposed and live at
OL,15,Fthe same time while the adaptor was
OL,16,Fplugged in.
OL,18,FThis means users could come into
OL,19,Fcontact with up to 240 volts of
OL,20,Felectricity, posing a serious risk of
OL,21,Felectric shock.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G2/10
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,315,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31403
SC,0003
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F314A1785383018
OL,3,C'Highly dangerous' travel adaptors
OL,4,Cfound for sale to UK consumers
OL,6,FIn the most serious circumstances,
OL,7,Fsuch as if someone were to touch the
OL,8,Fpins with wet hands, the consequences
OL,9,Fcould be fatal, the charity warned.
OL,11,FThe plug pins on all eight universal
OL,12,Ftravel adaptors also failed to meet
OL,13,Fthe dimensional and mechanical
OL,14,Fstrength requirements, meaning that
OL,15,Fthey could break off inside a socket.
OL,17,FIf a user instinctively tried to
OL,18,Fremove the broken pin, they could be
OL,19,Fexposed to a serious risk of electric
OL,20,Fshock.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G3/10
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
